            "title": "Banking Bellwethers Kick Off Earnings, Fed Chair's Speech In Focus",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\">Get ahead of the market by subscribing to Seeking Alpha's Wall Street Week Ahead, a preview of key events scheduled for the coming week. The newsletter keeps you informed of the biggest stories set to make headlines, including upcoming IPOs, investor days, earnings reports, and conference presentations.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Wall Street regained some momentum on Friday after the AI trade came under pressure on Thursday amid revenue concerns surrounding OpenAI (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/OPENAI\" title=\"OpenAI\">OPENAI</a>). Reports indicated that OpenAI's annualized revenue reached $50B at the end of September, below the $68B figure reported the previous month. On the economic front, consumer sentiment fell more than expected in October's initial reading as inflation expectations accelerated.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">The next week will kick off with IMF meetings beginning Monday. Existing home sales data for September will be released on Tuesday. On Wednesday, CPI data for September will be released with Retail sales and PPI data for the month the following day; initial jobless claims are also due on Thursday. Fed Chair Kevin Warsh’s speech is due on Friday, which will also be keenly watched out for by investors.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Banking bellwethers will kick off third-quarter earnings next week. Firms including JPMorgan (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/JPM\" title=\"JPMorgan Chase &amp; Co.\">JPM</a>), Morgan Stanley (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MS\" title=\"Morgan Stanley\">MS</a>), Citigroup (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/C\" title=\"Citigroup Inc.\">C</a>), and Goldman Sachs (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/GS\" title=\"The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc.\">GS</a>) are scheduled to report their results.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">______________________________________________________________</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Earnings 